Spec: Semester view

Purpose:
  A multi-column vertical list calendar (wall planner) showing one semester on one desktop screen. Each month is a
  column and each day is a row.

Owns:
  ./semester_view.py

Must:
  The semester periods are the four periods of academic year `2026-2027`, with semesters spanning the period groups
  `2026-08-01` to `2026-12-31` and `2027-01-01` to `2027-07-31`.
  The container is a CSS grid whose `grid-template-columns` is `repeat(`, one column per month of the selected
  semester, `, 1fr)`, and `gap: 10px`. A semester of five months renders five columns.
  The container height is `100vh` minus the header height, so a 1080p screen shows the whole semester without vertical
  or horizontal scrolling.
  The view is desktop-only and has no mobile responsiveness.
  Each month is a flex column (`display: flex; flex-direction: column`) with the month name as header at its top.
  Each month contains one row per day of that month, and each row has `flex: 1` so all rows share height equally.
  A day row shows the weekday abbreviation, the date number and a wider space for lesson indicators.
  Lessons appear as inline-block squares of `12px` by `12px` colored by their course.
  Hovering a square shows lesson details through a pure CSS tooltip that does not change the row height.
  Holidays are visibly distinguished on their day row and show their name.
  For the admin, clicking a day row opens the dialog specified in ./day-dialog.sdd.

Example:
  semester 1: `2026-08` to `2026-12`
  columns: `repeat(5, 1fr)`
  semester 2: `2027-01` to `2027-07`
  columns: `repeat(7, 1fr)`

Depends on:
  ./models.sdd
  ./day-dialog.sdd

Tasks:
  [ ] Render the static month columns and day rows
  [ ] Render lesson squares and CSS tooltips from the database
  [ ] Render holidays
  [x] Decide the semester start and range, since the layout is fixed at six months